# The image build context is the repository root (docker/Dockerfile).
#
# First and foremost: `.env` holds real key material and must never reach a
# layer — an image keeps every file ever copied into it, in its history, for
# anyone who can pull it (ADR 020).
.env
.env.*

# Rebuilt inside the image, or of no use to it.
node_modules
dist
coverage
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.log

# Documentation, tests, the evaluation harness (with its CUAD download,
# hundreds of MB) and the server scripts: not needed to build or run anything. The load tests'
# stub and k6 scripts are mounted into their containers, not baked in.
docs
test
eval
deploy
plan.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
